Article 12 Chinese citizens shall not be allowed to exit the country under any of the following circumstances:
(1) They do not hold valid exit and entry documents or refuse to or evade undergoing border inspection;
(2) They are sentenced to criminal punishment and the sentence has not been fully executed, or they are criminal suspects or defendants in criminal cases;
(3) They are involved in unsettled civil cases and the People's Court has decided that they shall not be allowed to exit the country;
(4) They have been subject to criminal punishment for impairing border (frontier) administration or have been repatriated by other countries or regions due to illegal exit, illegal stay or illegal employment, and the prescribed period during which exit is prohibited has not expired;
(5) They may endanger national security and interests, and the relevant competent department of the State Council has decided that they shall not be allowed to exit the country; or
(6) Other circumstances under which exit is prohibited as provided by laws or administrative regulations.

Article 56 Where a means of transportation is under any of the following circumstances, it shall not be allowed to exit or enter China; if it has already departed from a port, it may be ordered to return:
(1) exiting or entering China without examination and approval upon departure from or arrival at a port;
(2) changing the port of exit or entry without approval;
(3) being suspected of carrying persons who are not allowed to exit or enter China, requiring examination and verification;
(4) being suspected of carrying articles that endanger national security, interests, and public order, requiring examination and verification;
(5) refusing to accept other forms of management by the exit-entry border inspection authority.
After the circumstances listed in the preceding paragraph disappear, the exit-entry border inspection authority shall immediately release the relevant means of transportation.

Article 59 Any person suspected of violating exit/entry administration may be interrogated on the spot; after on-the-spot interrogation, if under any of the following circumstances, may be further interrogated according to law:
(1) being suspected of illegally exiting or entering China;
(2) being suspected of assisting others to illegally exit or enter China;
(3) a foreigner being suspected of unlawful residence or unlawful employment;
(4) being suspected of endangering national security and interests, disrupting public order, or engaging in other illegal or criminal activities.
On-the-spot interrogation and continued interrogation shall be conducted in accordance with the procedures prescribed in the People's Police Law of the People's Republic of China.
Where the public security organ of the local people's government at or above the county level or the exit-entry border inspection authority needs to summon a person suspected of violating exit/entry administration, the relevant provisions of the Law of the People's Republic of China on Public Security Administration Penalties shall be followed.

Article 61 Where a foreigner is under any of the following circumstances, detention for investigation shall not be applied, and the scope of his/her activities may be restricted:
(1) suffering from a serious disease;
(2) being pregnant or breastfeeding her own infant under one year of age;
(3) being under 16 years of age or at or above 70 years of age;
(4) other circumstances under which detention for investigation is inappropriate.
A foreigner whose activities are restricted shall undergo investigation as required, and shall not leave the restricted area without approval of the public security organ. The period of restriction on the scope of activities shall not exceed 60 days. For a foreigner whose nationality and identity are unknown, the period of restriction on the scope of activities shall be calculated from the date on which his/her nationality and identity are ascertained.

Article 62 Where a foreigner is under any of the following circumstances, he/she may be repatriated:
(1) being ordered to leave China within a specified period but failing to do so;
(2) being under any of the circumstances of not being allowed to enter China;
(3) illegally residing or working;
(4) violating this Law or other laws or administrative regulations and need to be repatriated.
Other overseas persons under any of the circumstances listed in the preceding paragraph may be repatriated according to law.
A person who has been repatriated shall not be allowed to enter China within one to five years from the date of repatriation.

Article 71 Whoever commits one of the following acts shall be fined not less than 1,000 yuan but not more than 5,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, shall be detained for not less than five days but not more than 10 days, and may also be fined not less than 2,000 yuan but not more than 10,000 yuan:
(1) exiting or entering China by using forged, altered, or fraudulently obtained exit/entry documents;
(2) exiting or entering China by using another person's exit/entry documents;
(3) evading exit/entry border inspection;
(4) illegally exiting or entering China by other means.

Article 76 A warning shall be given, and a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan may also be imposed, under any of the following circumstances:
(1) A foreigner refuses to accept the inspection of his/her exit/entry documents by a public security organ;
(2) A foreigner refuses to submit his/her residence permit for examination;
(3) Failing to register the birth or report the death of a foreigner in accordance with the relevant provisions;
(4) Failing to go through the formalities for alteration when the registered items in a foreigner's residence permit have changed, in accordance with the relevant provisions;
(5) A foreigner within Chinese territory fraudulently uses another person's exit/entry documents;
(6) Failing to register in accordance with the provisions of the second paragraph of Article 39 of this Law.
Where a hotel fails to register the accommodation of a foreigner in accordance with the relevant provisions, it shall be punished in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Public Security Administration Punishments Law of the People's Republic of China; where it fails to submit the information on foreigner accommodation registration to a public security organ in accordance with the relevant provisions, a warning shall be given; if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than 1,000 yuan but not more than 5,000 yuan shall be imposed.

Article 82 A warning shall be given, and a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan may also be imposed, under any of the following circumstances:
(1) Disrupting the administration of the port restricted zone;
(2) Foreign crew members or their accompanying family members go ashore without completing the formalities for temporary entry;
(3) Embarking on or disembarking from a foreign vessel without going through the formalities for a boarding certificate.
Where a person violates the provision of subparagraph (1) of the preceding paragraph, if the circumstances are serious, he/she may also be detained for not less than five days but not more than ten days.

Article 83 Where a means of transportation falls under any of the following circumstances, the person in charge thereof shall be fined not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 50,000 yuan:
(1) It leaves or enters China without being cleared by inspection or changes the port of exit/entry without approval;
(2) It fails to truthfully declare information such as crew members, passengers, goods or articles in accordance with the relevant provisions, or refuses to assist in exit/entry border inspection;
(3) It embarks or disembarks persons, loads or unloads goods or articles in violation of the provisions on exit/entry border inspection.
Where a means of transportation for exit/entry carries persons who are not allowed to exit or enter China, the person in charge thereof shall be fined not less than 5,000 yuan but not more than 10,000 yuan for each person carried. If the person in charge of the means of transportation proves that he/she has taken reasonable preventive measures, the punishment may be mitigated or exempted.

Article 84 Where a means of transportation falls under any of the following circumstances, the person in charge thereof shall be fined not less than 2,000 yuan but not more than 20,000 yuan:
(1) A Chinese or foreign vessel, without approval, sidles up alongside a foreign vessel;
(2) A foreign vessel or aircraft within Chinese territory operates not according to the prescribed routes or airlines;
(3) A vessel or aircraft exiting or entering China, in violation of the relevant provisions, sails or flies into an area other than a port open to the outside world.

Article 85 Where a staff member performing the duty of exit/entry administration commits any of the following acts, he/she shall be given a sanction according to law:
(1) In violation of laws or administrative regulations, issuing entry/entry documents such as visas, foreigner stay or residence permits to foreigners who do not meet the prescribed conditions;
(2) In violation of laws or administrative regulations, examining, verifying, and clearing persons or means of transportation that do not meet the prescribed conditions for exit or entry;
(3) Disclosing personal information known during exit/entry administration, infringing upon the lawful rights and interests of the parties;
(4) Failing to turn over to the State treasury the fees collected according to law, fines imposed, and illegal gains or illegal property confiscated, in accordance with the relevant provisions;
(5) Illegally sharing, appropriating, or misappropriating the money or property confiscated, detained, or the fees collected;
(6) Other acts of abusing power, neglecting duties, engaging in malpractices for personal gain, or failing to perform statutory duties according to law.
